title: jj as a Second VCS Backend
status: implemented
created: 2026-11-22
author: Luke Carrier
context: "Litterbox pairs a sandbox with a VCS branch. `adrs/2026-11-19-decouple-vcs-from-orchestration` put that pairing behind `vcs::Vcs` (`crates/agentkit-litterbox/src/vcs/mod.rs:32-211`) and named `vcs::jj` as the later second implementation (`vcs/mod.rs:5-6`). The module does not exist. `GitVcs` is the only implementation: it reports `ConflictModel::Blocking`, `op_log: false`, `BindingSupport::Copied` and `ExportSupport::None` (`vcs/git/scm.rs:447-455`), returns an empty mask (`:486-488`) and refuses `bound_root` (`:490-500`).\n\n`adrs/2026-11-22-adopt-rewritten-branches` built the source-state plan and the host workflow on Git. The reconciler (`orchestrator/reconcile.rs:116-140`) reads `ensure_refs`, `synced`, `tip`, `sandbox_tip`, `tree` and `is_ancestor`, and executes `AdoptHistory`, `AdoptContent`, `Snapshot`, `Block` and `Proceed`. `GitVcs` implements `report`, `stage`, `finish` and `discard_stage` in `vcs/git/reconcile.rs`, where staging is a linked worktree plus `merge-tree --write-tree --merge-base=<synced>` (`:62-207`). Nothing in the contract names a Git type: `Revision` and `TreeId` are opaque.\n\n`adrs/2026-11-21-hide-vcs-metadata-from-sandboxes` added the binding: `StoredSandbox.binding` with a legacy read of `Copied` (`metadata_store.rs:29-54`), `[vcs.<tool>]` as an untyped map in the local override (`config.rs:343-356`, `:483`), and `.git` and `.jj` masks in all three compute backends (`backends/bubblewrap/backend.rs:162`, `backends/docker/backend.rs:259`, `backends/seatbelt/policy.rs:232-245`). It deferred this ADR: the selector `[vcs] tool`, the `[vcs.jj]` section and the backend that makes either meaningful.\n\nThe map `maps/2026-11-18-litterbox-vcs-history-sync` settles the behaviour. T-001 proves jj hosts one workspace per sandbox; its `jj git export` step belongs to the non-colocated bridge the map assumes and disappears under the co-located clone described below. T-002 proves bubblewrap and Docker hide `.jj` under a bound workspace; T-018 proves Seatbelt denies it by rule. T-019 and T-021 settle what this ADR inherits: the sandbox never merges, it adopts when its workspace matches its own branch, it holds the shared branch when it does not, and a conflicted shared-branch revision is held rather than adopted. T-022 settles the model-facing report.\n\nThe store model here is simpler than the map's non-colocated bridge. `vcs/jj/<slug>` is a self-contained, co-located jj clone — jj's repository and its Git backend in one directory — symmetric with the git backend's `vcs/git/<slug>` (`vcs/git/path.rs:3-6`). A project uses one store or the other, never both, and jj's Git backend is internal to the clone. Because the clone is co-located, jj bookmarks and Git branches are the same refs: no `jj git import` or `jj git export` runs, and the user's checkout fetches from and pushes to the clone's `.git` directly. jj is remote-only: `snapshot-mode` is `[vcs.git]`'s alone (`domain/mod.rs:23-27` names it, default `Remote`), and jj has no direct mode.\n\nThe staging sequence is verified, not assumed. A probe against the installed jj 0.47.1 (`/tmp/opencode/jj-staging-probe`) shows `jj new <synced>` then `jj restore --from <tip>` builds each side as a child of `synced`, and `jj new <theirs'> <ours'>` forms a merge whose conflict set matches `git merge-tree --write-tree --merge-base=<synced>` (both report one path), whose markers name `synced` as the base, and which leaves the sandbox commit and the shared bookmark untouched with only scoped operations in the op log.\n\nTwo facts shape the mechanism. jj 0.47.1 is already on `PATH` (via nix) and no jj crate appears in any `Cargo.toml`; `jj-lib` has no stable API (31 breaking releases, roughly 500 breaking changes in 11 versions, self-described experimental), so the backend shells out to the `jj` binary and pins a minimum version. And `[vcs] tool` is not a typed field: `ProjectFile.vcs` is a map, so the selector must either be typed or read from the map, and its absence is a hard error at `open`, not a Git fallback."
problem: "Litterbox has one VCS backend. A workspace cannot select jj, no record says which tool owns a sandbox, and nothing creates a jj clone, a per-sandbox workspace, the shared branch, or a host staging workspace. The pieces jj needs already exist: opaque revisions, a `Blocking` conflict model, a held shared branch, a host staging workflow, records that carry a binding, and `.git` and `.jj` masks on every compute backend. The missing work is one selector, one record field, one refusal path and one backend."
goals[5]:
  - "A workspace selects jj in its untracked local override and creates a jj sandbox from it."
  - "A jj sandbox snapshots, adopts a rewritten history, adopts a rewritten tree when clean, and holds the shared branch when dirty."
  - "The sandbox's main workspace is never conflicted and stays buildable; the divergence is staged on the host for the user."
  - "A conflicted shared-branch revision is held rather than adopted, and the hold is reported to the model."
  - "Git-backed sandboxes behave as today; the Git backend is unchanged."
nonGoals[6]:
  - "Agent-side conflict resolution (the map's T-023)."
  - "Native conflicts in the main workspace and a `Conflicted` merge state."
  - "Placing jj's repository or `.jj` metadata inside the user's checkout; the clone lives in Litterbox's data directory."
  - "`Deferred` conflict emulation, git notes, or bookkeeping refs in the user's repository."
  - "History and undo beyond what the jj operation log already keeps."
  - "Any change to `GitVcs` or `vcs::git`, including the marker scan T-022 describes as Git's safety net."
requirements[18]{id,title,slug,description}:
  FR-001,"The tool selector",tool-selector,"A workspace names its VCS with `[vcs] tool` in the untracked `.agentkit/litterbox/config.local.toml`; the value is `git` or `jj`. It is required and there is no fallback: with no selector, `open` fails before any backend is built, and the error names the file and both values. The committed `.agentkit/litterbox/config.toml` cannot set it: a `[vcs]` key there is ignored with a notice naming it, as `[vcs.<tool>]` sections already are (`config.rs:456-462`)."
  FR-002,"Typed sections",vcs-sections,"`[vcs.git]` keeps `snapshot-mode` and `binding`; `snapshot-mode` is Git's alone. `[vcs.jj]` is typed in `vcs::jj` with `deny_unknown_fields`, carries only `binding`, and has no `snapshot-mode`; a mode for jj is refused. An unknown key, a non-table value or a value the tool does not accept is refused naming the section and the accepted values, as `vcs.git` already is (`vcs/git/config.rs:13-35`). The selected tool's section supplies its binding."
  FR-003,"The recorded tool",recorded-tool,"`StoredSandbox` gains `vcs: Option<String>` with a default and an accessor that reads an absent field as `git`, exactly as `binding` reads as `Copied` (`metadata_store.rs:29-54`). Create writes the selected tool. Repair preserves the recorded value rather than the configured one. Reading a record never rewrites it."
  FR-004,"A record this process cannot serve",tool-mismatch,"The orchestrator holds one backend, built once at open. Every operation that reads or writes a sandbox's source refuses, before any VCS call, when the record's `vcs` is not the selected tool: the error names the record's tool, the selected tool and the file that selects it. `list` reports such a record with the mismatch as its reason and does not pair it with a branch. No operation serves a jj record with the Git backend or the reverse."
  FR-005,"The jj clone",jj-clone,"`JjVcs` owns one clone per project at `vcs/jj/<slug>`: a self-contained, co-located jj repository cloned from the user's repository and Git-backed (jj's default storage). Its `.git` is the Git view Litterbox and the user's checkout exchange. jj creates a `default` workspace with the clone; Litterbox never uses it as a sandbox and never reports it. Each sandbox is `jj workspace add` at `vcs/jj/<slug>/workspaces/<name>`. The clone sits beside the git backend's `vcs/git/<slug>`; a project uses one or the other, never both."
  FR-006,"Three revisions",three-revisions,"Each sandbox addresses three revisions: the shared branch as the bookmark `litterbox/<name>`, the `theirs` side; the sandbox branch as the workspace's working-copy commit, the `ours` side; and the synced revision, a Git ref in the clone (`refs/litterbox/synced/<name>`), as what both sides last agreed on and the merge base. Moving the sandbox branch or the synced revision never moves the shared bookmark, and no operation merges in the sandbox."
  FR-007,"The Git view",git-view,"The clone's `.git` is the only Git view, and because the clone is co-located, jj bookmarks and Git branches are the same refs: no `jj git import` or `jj git export` runs. Creating or moving the bookmark `litterbox/<name>` is immediately the branch `refs/heads/litterbox/<name>` in the clone's `.git`, and a push to that branch is immediately the bookmark. Only the shared branch is a bookmark; `synced` is a record field and the sandbox branch is the working-copy commit, so no Litterbox bookkeeping appears in `refs/heads/*`. `state_path` names the clone's `.git`, and `expose` adds it to the user's checkout as a remote, as the git backend exposes its bare store."
  FR-008,"Prepare",prepare,"`prepare` creates the clone when absent, clones the user's repository, creates the shared bookmark at the base revision, records the sandbox branch and `synced` at that revision, adds the workspace, and returns the base revision as `Prepared`. It refuses when a workspace of that name already exists and names the existing path. A failure in any step leaves no bookmark or workspace behind."
  FR-009,"Snapshot",snapshot,"`snapshot` commits the staged tree on the sandbox branch and returns the revision. Under `Bound` the workspace is the sandbox itself, so jj snapshots it directly; under `Copied` the sandbox's copy is written into the workspace and jj snapshots that. An unchanged tree creates no commit. The shared bookmark moves only through `advance`. The commit is a compare-and-swap against the revision the plan read, abandoned and replanned under the same bounded retry the Git path uses (`orchestrator/reconcile.rs:88-99`). The sandbox workspace never gains a `.git`."
  FR-010,"Adoption and the hold",adoption-and-hold,"The plan stays the orchestrator's and is not duplicated: `orchestrator/source.rs` decides `AdoptHistory`, `AdoptContent`, `Snapshot`, `Block` and `Proceed` from the four trees. jj supplies the steps the plan names: `set_synced` records an adopted revision, `set_sandbox_tip` moves the sandbox branch, `advance` moves the shared bookmark (the branch), `observe` builds the tree a snapshot would commit without committing it, and `is_ancestor` answers the `Pending` exit. The conflict model is `Blocking`, as for Git, so the plan's `Merge`, `Resolve` and `Abort` steps are never selected."
  FR-011,"A conflicted shared-branch revision",conflicted-tip-fallback,"When the shared-branch revision carries conflicts the sandbox adopts nothing. On every operation that reads source state the reconciler asks `Vcs::conflicts` for the shared branch (`vcs/mod.rs:119`). A non-empty answer holds the sandbox at `synced` and its own branch, leaves the shared bookmark where it is, and reports the hold; tools still run and snapshots continue on the sandbox branch. `Error::Unsupported` means the backend has no conflict check and is read as no conflict; any other error fails the operation. jj answers from `jj resolve --list -r <rev>` or the `conflict` commit template (T-022). The hold is derived per operation and writes no record."
  FR-012,"The workspace block",workspace-block,"Every MCP tool that operates on one sandbox appends a `workspace` block to its result, as `success_with_recovery` appends the recovery block (`mcp.rs:631-641`). The block carries `state` (`clean` or `held`), `reason`, `synced`, `branch`, `sandbox`, `conflicts` and `next`. A held conflicted tip reports `held`, reason `shared branch is conflicted`, the synced revision, the shared-branch tip, the conflicted paths and the next step the user takes. A divergence the record holds (`Merge::Pending`) reports `held` with its own reason. The block writes nothing and is derived from the operation's post-plan state."
  FR-013,"Report and stage",staging,"`report` names the divergence and the paths that would conflict without writing a ref or a file in any checkout. `stage` creates a jj workspace at `vcs/jj/<slug>/reconcile/<name>` and builds the conflict there: `jj new <synced>` then `jj restore --from <branch-tip>` forms the `theirs` side, `jj new <synced>` then `jj restore --from <sandbox>` forms the `ours` side, and `jj new <theirs'> <ours'>` forms the merge. The merge's common ancestor is `synced`, its conflict set matches `git merge-tree --write-tree --merge-base=<synced>`, and neither the sandbox commit nor the shared bookmark moves. It refuses when a staging workspace already exists for the sandbox and names the existing path."
  FR-014,"Finish and discard",finish-and-discard,"`finish` refuses while the staging workspace holds uncommitted or unresolved paths, requires the staged revision to descend from the shared-branch tip, and moves the shared bookmark to it when no checkout holds the branch. When the user's checkout holds it, `finish` returns `Finished::Deferred` with the command the user runs. `discard_stage` removes the staging workspace and the duplicated commits and leaves the shared bookmark, the sandbox branch and `synced` where they were. No abort is a repository-wide `jj op restore`."
  FR-015,"Masking and binding",masking,"`masked_paths` returns `.jj`. Under `Copied` the workspace is an archive of a tree and therefore holds no `.jj`. Under `Bound` the workspace is the sandbox's jj workspace, non-colocated so it holds `.jj` and no `.git`; the compute backend masks `.jj` with a tmpfs on bubblewrap, an empty volume on Docker and a deny rule on Seatbelt (`backends/bubblewrap/backend.rs:162`, `backends/docker/backend.rs:259`, `backends/seatbelt/policy.rs:232-245`). `JjVcs` reports `BindingSupport::Both`; a compute backend that cannot mask still refuses `Bound` at validation, before a sandbox exists."
  FR-016,"Capabilities",capabilities,"`JjVcs` reports `ConflictModel::Blocking`, `op_log: true`, `BindingSupport::Both` and `ExportSupport::GitExport` (`vcs/capabilities.rs`). Only the orchestrator reads them, so reporting them adds no surface."
  FR-017,"Removal",removal,"`delete_branch` removes the sandbox workspace, the shared bookmark (the branch), and the `synced` ref. `prune` removes workspaces whose bookmark is gone and releases the clone once no `litterbox/*` bookmark remains, so deleting the last sandbox through `Bound` or the Git view is what triggers it (`orchestrator/service.rs:576-582`). `sandboxes` reports the sandbox names the clone exposes and never `default`. The branch remains the authoritative record of which sandboxes exist."
  FR-018,"The boundary",boundaries,"`vcs::jj` imports `vcs` and `vcs::git_common` and never `vcs::git`; `vcs::git` and `vcs::git_common` never import `vcs::jj`. `arch-lint.toml` gains the `litterbox-vcs-jj` scope, adds it to the deny lists that already name the Git scopes and to the `litterbox-vcs` deny list, adds it to the `litterbox-compose` allow list, and adds the `[[independent]]` rule over `litterbox-vcs-git` and `litterbox-vcs-jj` (`arch-lint.toml:442-465`). `hack/arch-lint-negative.sh` gains a case for each direction. These are the rules `adrs/2026-11-19-decouple-vcs-from-orchestration` FR-007 and FR-008 reserved for the first jj file."
nonFunctional[5]{id,title,slug,description}:
  NFR-001,"Backends stay apart",backends-apart,"No file under `vcs/jj` names `vcs::git` or a Git type, and no file under `vcs/git` or `vcs/git_common` names jj. `vcs::git_common` stays Git-specific and imports neither backend. `arch-lint check` passes and `bash hack/arch-lint-negative.sh` fails on each new case for the reason the case expects."
  NFR-002,"Git is unchanged",git-unchanged,"With `[vcs] tool = 'git'`, every operation behaves as it does today: the Git suite passes unchanged, the Git smoke passes under both `snapshot-mode` values, and no Git ref, file, message or error changes. A record with no `vcs` is a Git record and keeps working. `GitVcs` gains no code. The only Git-visible change is the new required selector at `open`."
  NFR-003,"One clone, one writer",clone-serialisation,"Snapshot, bookmark moves and staging serialise on a lock over the clone, because every workspace shares one jj repository. No abort or restore is a repository-wide command."
  NFR-004,"Local and lazy",local-and-lazy,"The backend uses no network: the clone is local. Source state is read when an operation plans, never by a watcher or a timer. A read on a sandbox whose branch has not moved costs a tip read and a conflict check, not a workspace materialisation."
  NFR-005,"The gates",gates,"`cargo test -p agentkit-litterbox`, `cargo clippy -p agentkit-litterbox --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `arch-lint check` and `bash hack/arch-lint-negative.sh` pass. The smoke runs the jj selector end to end and the Git selector under both `snapshot-mode` values."
acceptance[8]{id,title,slug,description}:
  AC-001,"A jj sandbox through the workflow",jj-workflow,"With `[vcs] tool = 'jj'`: create a sandbox; run a tool; snapshot; rewrite the shared bookmark with a tree-identical rewrite and see adoption with no new commit; rewrite its content while the workspace is clean and see the new content; edit the sandbox and rewrite the content and see the hold with the bookmark unchanged and a `held` block; stage; resolve in the staging workspace and commit; finish; see the bookmark moved and the next operation adopt; stage again, discard, and see the bookmark untouched."
  AC-002,"The main workspace stays buildable",main-workspace-buildable,"Across AC-001, after every step `conflicts` on the sandbox branch is empty, the sandbox workspace holds no conflict markers, and a command in the sandbox succeeds."
  AC-003,"A conflicted tip is held",conflicted-tip-held,"Point the shared bookmark at a conflicted revision. The next operation adopts nothing, the sandbox stays on `synced`, a tool still runs, and the workspace block reports `held` with reason `shared branch is conflicted` and the conflicted paths."
  AC-004,"The branch is the surface",branch-surface,"After a snapshot the clone's `.git` has `refs/heads/litterbox/<name>` at the sandbox's revision and no Litterbox bookkeeping branch under `refs/heads/*`. `litterbox remote add` followed by a fetch in the user's checkout reaches the bookmark."
  AC-005,"Masking under both bindings",masking-both-bindings,"A `Copied` jj sandbox holds no `.jj` anywhere in its workspace. A `Bound` jj sandbox sees `.jj` as an empty entry on bubblewrap and Docker and an inaccessible one on Seatbelt, and no read or write under it succeeds."
  AC-006,"The boundary holds",boundary-holds,"`arch-lint check` passes with the new scope and rules, `bash hack/arch-lint-negative.sh` fails on each new case, and no file in `vcs/jj` names a Git module while no file in `vcs/git` or `vcs/git_common` names jj."
  AC-007,"Legacy and refusals",legacy-and-refusals,"A record written before this change operates as a Git sandbox without being rewritten. A workspace with no `[vcs] tool` fails at `open` for every command, naming the file and both values. A record whose `vcs` differs from the selected tool refuses every source operation and `list` reports it with the mismatch."
  AC-008,"Git behaves as before",git-behaves,"The Git suite and the Git smoke pass unchanged under both `snapshot-mode` values with `[vcs] tool = 'git'`."
edgeCases[12]{id,title,slug,description}:
  EC-001,"A legacy record",legacy-record,"A record with no `vcs` reads as `git` and is never rewritten. Its `binding` and `merge` fields keep their existing meaning."
  EC-002,"A missing prerequisite",missing-prerequisite,"When the jj the backend needs is absent or below the pinned minimum, the operation fails with an error naming the prerequisite, and create leaves no clone, bookmark or workspace behind."
  EC-003,"A copied jj sandbox",copied-is-not-a-workspace,"Under `Copied` the sandbox directory is not a jj workspace and holds no `.jj`. A snapshot of it still lands a commit on the sandbox branch by writing the copy into the workspace, and the sandbox never gains `.jj` or `.git`."
  EC-004,"A duplicate workspace",duplicate-workspace,"`prepare` for a name whose workspace already exists refuses and names the path. It does not reuse, move or overwrite it."
  EC-005,"Conflicted and dirty at once",conflict-while-dirty,"A conflicted shared-branch revision while the sandbox has unsaved work is the conflicted-tip hold, not the divergence hold: nothing is adopted, no staging is suggested, tools run and snapshots continue on the sandbox branch."
  EC-006,"A push races a snapshot",push-races-snapshot,"Because the bookmark is the branch, a user's push and a snapshot race on the same ref. The compare-and-swap and bounded retry in FR-009 resolve it: a lost race is abandoned and replanned, and no operation proceeds against a tip the plan did not read."
  EC-007,"A second stage",second-stage,"A second `stage` for the same sandbox refuses and names the existing workspace path."
  EC-008,"A dirty staging workspace",dirty-staging,"`finish` refuses while the staging workspace holds uncommitted or unresolved paths and leaves the workspace and the bookmark alone."
  EC-009,"A workspace removed outside Litterbox",workspace-gone,"A record whose workspace directory is gone is `Missing` and repairs by re-adding the workspace at the shared-branch tip; the bookmark and `synced` are not moved."
  EC-010,"A bookmark removed outside Litterbox",bookmark-gone,"A sandbox whose bookmark is gone is `NotFound`. The operation fails and mints no bookmark or workspace."
  EC-011,"The default workspace",default-workspace,"`sandboxes` never reports `default`, `prune` never removes it, and work a user leaves in it is ignored by every Litterbox operation."
  EC-012,"A staging workspace outlives its sandbox",stale-staging,"Deleting a sandbox removes its staging workspace and its duplicated commits; a staging workspace whose directory is gone is pruned before the next stage, as the Git path prunes a stale worktree (`vcs/git/reconcile.rs:304-312`)."
